    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green).\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did to satisfy the registration-date rule:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's accepted on `POST /api/owners` and returned on the `Owner` response (which extends `OwnerFields`). The generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` pick it up automatically by name.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) column with getter/setter, plus a `toString` entry.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 When the supplied date is null, defaults it to the server's current date (`LocalDate.now()`), placed right alongside the existing telephone/email normalization in the create flow. A supplied date is left untouched.\n- **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column so the entity maps under the `ddl-auto=none` test profile.\n\nSerialization to the ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string is handled by Jackson's default `LocalDate` rendering, matching the tests' expectations (`today()` default, and preserved `\"2020-06-15\"`).",
